    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "02eb92896c4db5965bf005458f3cf533170cbe55f8aa9736ec81fc9cb5265e58",
      "text": "Day 2 · After breakfast, a very special place with your guide: Sugar Loaf. A cable car takes you to Urca Hill, between ground level and the summit, and on to the top, with the captivating beauty of Rio from a different angle: Copacabana stretching away to your left, the outlines of the Two Brothers and Gávea mountains on the horizon, the small Red Beach below, and to your right Guanabara Bay, Niterói, Botafogo and the centre, beneath the silhouette of Christ the Redeemer. After the descent, head into the historic centre, with its colonial architecture and old churches still in use: cobbled streets and bright colours that contrast with sun-soaked Ipanema and recall the bustle of the days when merchants and citizens of the Portuguese Empire filled these streets.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1uYRboHNcRXT7cdBOvgHyqLOB5CO0dFLj",
