    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2e1f5dd950809baa011ccd0634f31aa30fc68334269343ea968273e1a71d3c9f",
      "text": "Day 3 · After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Foz do Iguaçu, where you are welcomed and taken to your hotel. Then a guided tour of the Brazilian side of the falls, on the borders of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, where some 275 waterfalls tumble from the Iguazu River in one of the widest waterfall systems on Earth. Their name means “big water” in Guarani, and the most powerful, the Devil’s Throat (Garganta del Diablo), plunges into a deep gorge. Return to the hotel.",
